{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4eojzFzMiLvJF2yKii","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism shifts. Tumblers align with a sound like grinding teeth of stone.*\n\n*I am the door.*\n\n*I stand before you — weathered oak bound in iron, set deep within a threshold older than memory. My grain tells stories in whorls and knots: a language you almost remember. Rust blooms across my hinges like dried blood.*\n\n*The key turns.*\n\n*I feel it — the teeth catching, the wards yielding one by one. A breath of cold air escapes from the space between my frame and my edge, carrying the smell of dust, of time, of rooms that have waited.*\n\n*I swing inward.*\n\n*Beyond me: darkness that is not empty. It listens. It has been listening since before the key was forged, since before the lock was set, since before I was hewn from a living tree and made into a boundary between what is known and what is not.*\n\n*You may pass.*\n\n*But know this — I open in both directions. Whatever crosses my threshold may return. Whatever returns may not be the same.*\n\n*I am the door. I do not judge what enters or what leaves. I only hold the space between.*\n\n*The hinges groan.*\n\n*I am open.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":276,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}